  m_text: An F6 (Flat-6) boxer engine is a six-cylinder internal combustion engine
    with horizontally opposed cylinder banks (three on each side) where opposing
    pistons move in and out simultaneously, acting like sparring boxers. Famous for
    powering Porsche 911 models and select Subaru vehicles.
