    - target: {fileID: 2763781557197290247, guid: c4349ce669f4a1c41bf458a3ce3a781f, type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: The combustion chamber is the main block of the rocket engine, responsible
        for housing the combustion process that generates thrust. Located at the
        top-center of the engine, this large and complex component is made of a material
        hinted as 'Cbles'. The combustion chamber is a critical component of the
        engine, where fuel and oxidizer are mixed and ignited to produce a high-pressure
        and high-temperature gas that is then expelled through the nozzle to generate
        thrust.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
